<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;c&gt; 
tie @ary, "My::Class", "some", "el", "ems";
for (@ary) {
   some_code($_);
}
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

What if the loop is left by [DOC://last|&lt;tt&gt;last&lt;/tt&gt;] , [DOC://next|&lt;tt&gt;next&lt;/tt&gt;] , [DOC://redo|&lt;tt&gt;redo&lt;/tt&gt;] , [DOC://return|&lt;tt&gt;return&lt;/tt&gt;] or [DOC://goto|&lt;tt&gt;goto&lt;/tt&gt;] ?&lt;P&gt;


Does the code hooked into the tied array really catch all edge cases sufficiently for your progress-bar?
 &lt;P&gt;

&lt;H5&gt; edit&lt;/H5&gt;&lt;P&gt;

Is there any -&gt;DESTROY of the tied class being called? &lt;P&gt;


NB: As already told, be aware about restrictions on Perl versions. &lt;P&gt;

